// A build signed by a free Personal Team (an Apple ID in Xcode, no paid
// membership). Signing.local.xcconfig includes this file after its
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM line; see docs/signing.md.
//
// Bundle ids and `group.` App Groups are unique across all teams, and Xcode
// registers what it signs: these names stay apart from the shipped app's, so
// the Personal Team never takes one the paid team needs.
//
// Free accounts get neither Time Sensitive nor Communication Notifications
// (architecture §11): PersonalTeam.entitlements claims neither, so blocking
// notifications are ordinary ones and Focus comes from the Shortcuts
// automation (`gentbox focus on|off`) instead of INFocusStatusCenter.
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
GENTBOX_ENTITLEMENTS = Signing/PersonalTeam.entitlements
GENTBOX_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.eiluviann.gentbox.personal

// A macOS-style App Group, prefixed by the team id: never registered, and
// macOS 15 opens its container without a prompt. With no restricted
// entitlement left, the build needs no provisioning profile, so it does not
// expire weekly; only the certificate does, after a year.
GENTBOX_APP_GROUP = $(DEVELOPMENT_TEAM).com.eiluviann.gentbox
REGISTER_APP_GROUPS = NO
